This simplistic argument scan can produce false positives if a value for another flag matches the pattern (e.g., --label "--search"). This would cause the list wrapper to route to the search fallback, which would then fail to find a search term. Following repository guidelines for robust CLI argument parsing, use a whitelist of flags known to consume an additional argument to correctly skip them and handle various flag formats.

```suggestion
_rest_args_have_search() {
	while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
		case "$1" in
		--search|--search=*) return 0 ;;
		--repo|--state|--label|--assignee|--limit|--json|--jq|-q|--head|--base) shift 2 2>/dev/null || shift ;;
		--repo=*|--state=*|--label=*|--assignee=*|--limit=*|--json=*|--jq=*|--head=*|--base=*) shift ;;
		*) shift ;;
		esac
	done
	return 1
}
```

